    pr_ref:  # 44c6
    description: "Pre-existing julia const-emitter bugs, surfaced by the WI-jusus module-variable review (distinct from that slice, which correctly returns None for const_statement parents). (1) const a,b=1,2 emits ZERO const symbols (open_tuple LHS). (2) const K::Int=3 dropped/mis-named (typed_expression LHS). (3) const handler=5 clobbers a same-named cross-module function (bare-name registration beats the function's qualified suffix-match). Fix: reuse _julia_assignment_target_names(lhs) for const LHS extraction; for the clobber, a const value binding CAN be a legit call target (const f=()->… is callable), so keep it resolvable but add a function-preferring resolver tie-break OR module-qualified const names. Evidence: analyze_julia on 'module M; const a,b=1,2; end' -> zero const; 3-module file with const handler=5 (B) + function handler() (A) + caller (C) -> caller resolves to const:handler not the function."  # 44c6
    fields:  # 44c6
      statement: "Every valid Julia const declaration emits a const symbol for ALL declared names (including multi-name const a,b=1,2 and typed const K::Int=3), and a const value binding never wrongly clobbers a same-named cross-module function in call resolution."  # 44c6
      root_cause: "The const_statement emitter uses find_child_by_type(assignment,identifier) which finds no direct identifier for an open_tuple or typed_expression LHS (dropping multi-name and typed consts), and registers const under its BARE unqualified name so it EXACT-matches a bare foo() call and beats a same-named function module-qualified suffix-match."  # 44c6
